{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>This is its interpretation.</b> The reason he said thus in interpreting dreams is that he intended to give the speech of the interpretation dominion over the thought, for in this matter dreams follow the mouth, since the thought changes in accordance with the speech that holds sway over it. And specifically if he says ״זֶה פִּתְרוֹנוֹ״ — for by this he gives dominion to the speech. And similarly you will find that he spoke in this manner in interpreting Pharaoh's dream, as I shall explain there with the help of HaShem blessed be He."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:17.532283842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}